.TH VULNMATCH 1 "2026-11-04" "unheaded 3a1f1b55" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
vulnmatch \- Match the components a tree pins against OSV records and the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vulnmatch
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Match the components a tree pins against OSV records and the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-on\-findings
exit 1 when anything matched
.TP
.B \-\-json
print findings as JSON
.TP
.B \-\-kev\-file \fISTRING\fR
CISA KEV catalog, kev\-poller's latest.json
.TP
.B \-\-osv\-dir \fISTRING\fR
directory of OSV records, one *.json each
.TP
.B \-\-root \fISTRING\fR
tree to read lock data from (default .)
.TP
.B \-\-sbom \fISTRING\fR
also read sbom/go\-dependencies.json or sbom/rust\-dependencies.json
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exit codes: 0 scan complete, 1 findings (with \-\-fail\-on\-findings), 2 usage or scan error.
Reads local files only.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
vulnmatch \-\-root . \-\-osv\-dir pkg/threatfeed/osv/testdata/records \-\-kev\-file pkg/threatfeed/osv/testdata/kev.json
vulnmatch \-\-osv\-dir /var/tmp/osv \-\-kev\-file /var/lib/unheaded/threat\-feeds/cisa\-kev/latest.json \-\-fail\-on\-findings
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
